// AUTO-GENERATED from static/matchaTonoki-logo.svg (the drawn brand logo).
// Do not edit by hand — re-run the bake described in
// .agents/docs/project-status-2026-08-25c.md and paste the result.
//
// The stone is rebuilt as a bevelled slab with the artwork painted on its two
// faces, the way an enamel pin is made. Five things this bake depends on:
//
//   - The ink outline is NOT a painted layer. The base slab is ink-coloured
//     and the colour fills stop short of the silhouette, so the unpainted
//     margin showing around them IS the outline. One less layer, and the line
//     wraps the bevel instead of stopping dead at the edge.
//   - The colour grows 0.033 before being clipped, landing its edge at 0.045
//     from the silhouette — exactly where the bevel starts. Paint edge and
//     bevel crease then fall on the same line. Leave them apart and the result
//     is two concentric lines with a shading crease between them.
//   - That growth must stay well under the artwork's own ~0.078 inset. Flood
//     past it (0.14 was tried) and the paint jumps the band entirely, leaking
//     green into the tail curl and the stem, which are solid ink in the
//     drawing rather than outline.
//   - Front paint has the ink subtracted from it. Paint and ink are simplified
//     independently, so their shared edges diverge by up to the tolerance and
//     the paint pokes out from under the ink as a bright hairline. With the
//     ink punched out, that same mismatch exposes the slab, already ink-
//     coloured. Back paint is NOT punched — it carries no ink, and the holes
//     would show the slab through and give the reverse a face.
//   - Every paint layer is clipped to `silhouette.buffer(-BEVEL_SIZE)`. Paint
//     crossing the bevel would hang off the rounded edge in mid-air, so the
//     bevel is baked into the data; the two must change together.
//
// Contours are simplified at 0.6 artwork units. Coordinates are normalised to
// a 3.9-unit height, centred on the origin — the same space as the low-poly
// bake, so the scene's layout knobs carry over.

/** Bevel the paint was clipped against. Changing this alone WILL float the paint. */
export const MAGATAMA_ICON_BEVEL_SIZE = 0.045;

export interface MagatamaIconLayer {
  /** `base` is the slab; `front` and `back` are paint laid on its flat faces. */
  role: 'base' | 'front' | 'back';
  /** Steps of `paintGap` off the face. Colour fills sit at 1, the ink on 2. */
  tier: number;
  color: string;
  /** Polygons; each is `[outer, ...holes]`, each ring a flat `[x, y, …]`. */
  contours: number[][][];
}

